{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599702",
      "title": "The Component Lifecycle (Class-based Components Only!)",
      "sourceHash": "30969be21be1c6fa4c904b4e3029e2c6f6c2e7f458d4de1dbdf0ed0c9b15dc4c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "Now we know how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 6.15,
          "en": "we can generally build class-based components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.15,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "and how we can manage state and work with events, steer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 12.02,
          "en": "But what about side effects?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.02,
          "end": 15.52,
          "en": "As I mentioned, you can't use these react hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.52,
          "end": 19.91,
          "en": "in class-based components, so you can't use use effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.91,
          "end": 22.84,
          "en": "but class-based components have a concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.84,
          "end": 26.23,
          "en": "called the component life cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.23,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "And of course, every component technically has a life cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "It, for example, is rendered to the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "or remove from the DOM, but there are specific methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "you can add two class-based components to run code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 43.23,
          "en": "at different points in that life cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.23,
          "end": 47.2,
          "en": "And the first, most important life cycle method you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.2,
          "end": 48.96,
          "en": "to class-based components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.96,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "is to componentDidMount() method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.33,
          "end": 55.4,
          "en": "like render() that's a built in method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.4,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "which you can use as soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 59.96,
          "en": "as you extend the built in component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.96,
          "end": 61.57,
          "en": "which you import from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.57,
          "end": 64.24,
          "en": "And then you can add this method and React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.24,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "We'll call it for you when the component was just mounted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 70.57300000000001,
          "en": "but more on that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.47,
          "end": 73.13,
          "en": "Other live cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.13,
          "end": 74.77,
          "en": "methods you can add would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.77,
          "end": 79.28,
          "en": "componentDidUpdate() and componentWillUnmount().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.28,
          "end": 82.437,
          "en": "There are a couple of other less important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.437,
          "end": 85.85,
          "en": "to lifecycle methods, which will not take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.85,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "at here because these free lifecycle methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 93.13,
          "en": "are by far the most important and common ones.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.13,
          "end": 94.939,
          "en": "Now, as I said, componentDidMount()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.939,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "is called when a component is mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 102.03,
          "en": "So when it was evaluated and now rendered to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 107.03,
          "en": "It's basically the equivalent to using use EFFECT like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.66,
          "end": 110.3,
          "en": "You have your EFFECT function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.3,
          "end": 113.1,
          "en": "which I left out here with the free dots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.1,
          "end": 117.22999999999999,
          "en": "And then you have the array of dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.22999999999999,
          "end": 120.98,
          "en": "and every EFFECT function is executed when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.98,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "the component first is mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 125.86,
          "en": "But if you have no dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.86,
          "end": 128.27,
          "en": "if you have an empty dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.27,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "the EFFECT function is only executed in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 136.75,
          "en": "So adding use of fact with an empty dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.75,
          "end": 141.247,
          "en": "array is basically your equivalent to componentDidMount().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.25,
          "end": 144.82,
          "en": "And we're going to See componentDidMount()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.82,
          "end": 146.453,
          "en": "in action in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "You'll also have componentDidUpdate().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 155.2,
          "en": "This is called once a component was updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.2,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "So when something changed when your state changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "and the component was re-evaluated and re-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.89,
          "end": 166.68,
          "en": "this is basically your equivalent to use effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.68,
          "end": 171.43,
          "en": "with some dependencies, whenever the dependencies change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.43,
          "end": 174.64,
          "en": "the use EFFECT function re-executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.64,
          "end": 177.73,
          "en": "and the dependencies are re-evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.73,
          "end": 180.07,
          "en": "when the component is re-evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.07,
          "end": 181.89,
          "en": "and was rendered again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 182.83,
          "en": "Because you'll learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.83,
          "end": 186.72,
          "en": "that the effects are generally re-executed whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.72,
          "end": 190.23,
          "en": "a component re-rendered, if dependencies changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.23,
          "end": 193.717,
          "en": "So that's why this is basically your equivalent to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.717,
          "end": 195.71,
          "en": "componentDidDpdate().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.71,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "Now componentWillUnmount is called right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.78,
          "en": "before the component is removed from the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 206.463,
          "en": "and here the equivalent is basically the clean up function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.463,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "from use EFFECT that cleanup function is called right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 214,
          "en": "before the EFFECT function is executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "and also always again, when the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 220.023,
          "en": "is about to be removed from the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.91,
          "end": 225.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now again, let's take a closer look at that in action here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.17000000000002,
          "end": 228.7,
          "en": "And for this, I altered the project slightly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.7,
          "end": 231.55,
          "en": "attached you find the UserFinder component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.55,
          "end": 233.63,
          "en": "which you can add to your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.63,
          "end": 236.81,
          "en": "And now we need to go to the users component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.81,
          "end": 240.97,
          "en": "and dare get rid of the dummy users here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.97,
          "end": 244.41,
          "en": "And instead here, where we used the dummy users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.41,
          "end": 249.41,
          "en": "refer to this props users, because users are now passed in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 255.37,
          "en": "through props into this users component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.37,
          "end": 256.64,
          "en": "And now we just need to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.64,
          "end": 261.64,
          "en": "to the App component and use the UserFinder component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.43,
          "end": 266.71,
          "en": "and import user finder from components UserFinder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.71,
          "end": 268.71,
          "en": "Instead of users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.71,
          "end": 273.14,
          "en": "also add the UserFinder. Module.CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.14,
          "end": 274.803,
          "en": "which you also find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.75,
          "end": 277.46,
          "en": "And if you added all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.46,
          "end": 280.01,
          "en": "and you saved as you should see an application that looks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.01,
          "end": 284.88,
          "en": "like this, and here, if you type you now also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 288.53,
          "en": "filter this list down there with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.53,
          "end": 291.093,
          "en": "It's a very simple filter logic, which I added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.093,
          "end": 294.58,
          "en": "into UserFinder, and the UserFinder component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.58,
          "end": 298.9,
          "en": "is a functional component using multiple state slices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.9,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "and use EFFECT to manage the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 304.31,
          "en": "and to then filter the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.31,
          "end": 307.833,
          "en": "and pass the filtered users to the users component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.79,
          "end": 311.07,
          "en": "Now let's transform this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.07,
          "end": 314.08,
          "en": "to a class-based component to get an idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.08,
          "end": 318.503,
          "en": "on how these class-based components deal with side effects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}